    five notifications.
  - [1mDigest timing[0m uses one configured site-wide send hour rather than per-user timezones. A 5–50 person internal team is
    usually in one or two zones, and per-user scheduling is real complexity for little gain.
  - [1mReassignment[0m subscribes the new assignee but does not unsubscribe the old one — they were involved, and they can
    mute.
  - [1mDev email[0m uses Django's console backend, so nothing escapes locally.

  [1mTesting.[0m The service layer is where the value is, so that's where the tests concentrate: each service function emits
  exactly the expected event and subscription changes. Then fan-out (correct recipients, self excluded, muted excluded,
  inactive excluded), the email batcher (grouping, skip-if-already-read, retry idempotency, the failure cap), and
  view-level permission tests. Test-driven, per the workflow — these are pure functions over a database, which is about
  the easiest thing there is to write tests for first.

  [1mTooling.[0m This is a new project with nothing configured, and setting this up before any code exists is the cheapest it
  will ever be. I'd default to ruff + ruff format and mypy (matching your environment), and pytest + pytest-django with
  factory_boy. Your call on how far to go:
[38;5;246m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
← [38;5;16m[48;5;153m ☒ Tooling [39m[49m ☐ Section 3  ✔ Submit  →

[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mWhich tooling should be set up from the start? (These land in the spec's Global Constraints, so every later task [0m
[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231minherits them.)[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;114m[✔][39m [38;5;153mLint + autoformat (Recommended)[39m
  [38;5;246mruff and ruff format, configured strictly, plus mypy. Matches the Python setup in your config. Near-zero cost now, [39m
  [38;5;246mpainful to retrofit across a grown codebase.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m [ ] Unit test infra (Recommended)
  [38;5;246mpytest + pytest-django, factory_boy, a test layout and one passing fixture. Required for the TDD workflow, and the [39m
  [38;5;246mservice layer is the part that most needs it.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m [ ] End-to-end tests
  [38;5;246mPlaywright driving a real browser through login, task edit, and the notification bell. Catches the wiring that unit [39m
  [38;5;246mtests miss, but it's the slowest and most brittle tier to maintain.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m [ ] Mutation testing
  [38;5;246mmutmut or similar, to check the tests actually catch regressions. Genuinely useful for notification fan-out logic [39m
  [38;5;246mwhere a wrong filter silently sends to the wrong people — but slow and usually a later addition.[39m
